s:
Powers of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon while conducting joint sessions:
Approval of presidential decrees on appointment and dismissal of the Prime Minster and other members of the Government;
Approval of the presidential decree on declaration of martial law and state of emergency;
Consent to using the Armed Forces of the Republic of Tajikistan outside its borders in order to fulfill international obligations of Tajikistan;
Calling presidential elections;
Acceptance of the President's resignation;
Awarding the President with State prizes and conferring on him high military titles;
Consideration of the issue of the immunity of the President.

Powers of the Majlisi Milli:
Creation, abolition and modification of administrative-territorial units;
Election and recall of the Chairman, Deputy Chairmen, and judges of the Constitutional Court, the Supreme Court, and the Highest Economic Court upon the presentation of the President;
Decision on the issue of immunity deprivation of the Chairman, Deputy Chairmen, and judges of the Constitutional Court, Supreme Court and Highest Economic Court;
Giving consent to the appointment and dismissal of the General Procurator and his deputies;
Exercising other powers determined by the Constitution and law.

Powers of the Majlisi Namoyandagon:
Creation of the Central Commission for Elections and Referenda of the Republic Tajikistan, election and recall of the Chairman, Deputy Chairman, and members of the commission upon the presentation of the President;
Submission of bills and other important State and public issues for nation-wide debate;
Approval of socio-economic programs;
Authorization of disbursement and receipt of State credit;
Ratification and denouncement of international treaties;
Calling of a referendum;
Creation of courts;
Approval of State symbols;
Approval of State awards;
Approval of Presidential decrees on appointment and dismissal of the Chairman of the National Bank and his deputies;
Establishing of military titles, diplomatic ranks, and other special ranks and titles;
Establishing of the President's salary;
Exercising other powers determined by the Constitution and law.

Powers of the President:
Determines basic directions of the interior and foreign policy of the Republic;
Represents Tajikistan within the country and in international relations;
Creates and abolishes ministries and State committees;
Appoints and dismisses the Prime Minister and other members of the Government; presents decrees appointing and dismissing the Prime Minister and other members of the Government to the joint session of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon for approval;
Appoints and dismisses the Chairmen of the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast, oblasts, the city of Dushanbe, cities and rayons, [and] presents them for the approval of the appropriate Majlis of People's Deputies;
Annuls or suspends acts of organs of executive power in case they contradict the Constitution and laws;
Appoints and dismisses the Chairman of the National Bank, his deputies, and present relevant decrees for the approval of the Majlisi Namoyandagon;
Presents to the Majlisi Milli candidates for election and recall of Chairman, Deputy Chairmen, and judges of the Constitutional Court, Supreme Court and Higher Economic Court;
With the consent of the Majlisi Milli appoints and dismisses the General Procurator and his deputies;
Creates the executive apparatus of the President;
Creates the Security Council and leads it;
Appoints and dismisses judges of military courts, the court of the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast, oblasts , the city of Dushanbe, the city and rayon courts, and judges of economic courts of the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast, oblasts, and the city of Dushanbe;
Calls referendum, elections to the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon, [and] to local representative organs;
Signs laws;
Determines the monetary system and informs the Majlisi Milli and Majlisi Namoyandagon about it;
Administers the reserve fund;
Leads the conduct of foreign policy, signs international treaties and presents them for the approval of the Majlisi Namoyandagon;
Appoints the heads of diplomatic missions in foreign States and the representatives of the Republic to international organizations;
Accepts the credentials of the heads of foreign diplomatic missions;
Is the Supreme Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces of Tajikistan; appoints and dismisses commanders of the Armed Forces of Tajikistan;
Declares martial law during a realistic threat to national security and presents a corresponding decree for approval of the joint session of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon;
Uses the Armed Forces of the Republic of Tajikistan outside its borders in order to fulfill international obligations of Tajikistan with the consent of the joint session of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon;
Declares a state of emergency on the entire territory of the Republic or in individual locations with an immediate presentation of a corresponding decree for approval to the joint session of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon and notification of the United Nations;
Resolves issues of citizenship;
Grants political asylum;
Grants pardons;
Confers the highest titles, diplomatic ranks, [and] other special ranks and titles;
Awards citizens with State awards, prizes, and honorary titles of Tajikistan;
Executes other powers provided by the Constitution and laws.

Powers of the Constitutional Court:
Determining of the conformity to the Constitution of laws, joint legal acts of the Majlisi Milli and the Majlisi Namoyandagon, the President, Government, Supreme Court, Highest Economic Court, and other State and social organs, as well as agreements of Tajikistan which have not entered into legal force;
Resolving disputes between State organs regarding their competences;
Execution of other powers determined by the Constitution and laws.
